    skos:altLabel "SE_SE4A_TP" ;
    skos:definition """The EIC code represents an Aggregated Area defined by the TSO and used as a Technical Profile within the MARI and PICASSO balancing platforms.
The area is a virtual aggregation of several bidding zones and is used for modelling operational constraints and capacity limitations, in particular to limit flow variations over HVDC interconnections.
"""@en ;
